### 2.3 Completely Unprotected Server RPC Endpoints (Authorization Bypass / IDOR)
In **[data.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/server/data.ts)**, sensitive server functions do not inspect the session token or verify caller roles:
- `fetchUsersFn`: Any anonymous client or student can dump the entire users table (emails, names, roles, batch IDs).
- `createUserFn`: Any client can create permanent faculty/teacher accounts.
- `deleteUserFn`: Any client can delete student and teacher accounts.
- `createAssignmentFn` / `deleteAssignmentFn`: Any student can delete assignments and cascade-delete attempts.
- `updateStudentStatusFn`: Any caller can alter student status flags.

