## 3. Database & Data Architecture Deficiencies

### 3.1 Raw Audio Stored as Base64 in MongoDB Documents
- **[useAudioRecorder.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/features/practice/hooks/useAudioRecorder.ts#L177-L184)** & **[attempt.service.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/server/services/attempt.service.ts#L67)**:
  Audio recording Blobs are converted to Base64 strings and written directly into the `attempts` collection in MongoDB.
- **Production Risk**: Audio recordings easily exceed 3–10MB. MongoDB has a strict 16MB document limit. Storing raw audio inside BSON documents bloats indexes, exhausts server RAM cache, and causes query timeouts.
- **Production Requirement**: Store media files in S3/Cloudflare R2/GCS and store only the secure object URL in MongoDB.

### 3.2 Global Module Completion Collision
- **[attempt.service.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/server/services/attempt.service.ts#L76)** & **[module.service.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/server/services/module.service.ts#L70)**:
  When a student completes a module, the system updates `modules.updateOne({ id: payload.moduleId }, { $set: { completed: true } })`.
- **Bug**: The `completed` boolean is stored on the global module document. When Student A finishes Module 1, Module 1 is marked as completed for **all students across the school**. Module progress must be tracked in a per-student progress record or derived from user attempts.

### 3.3 Status Recalculation Resets Manual Teacher Actions
- **[student.service.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/server/services/student.service.ts#L51-L71)** & **[student.service.ts:L112-L132](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/server/services/student.service.ts#L112-L132)**:
  When fetching a student or roster, status is dynamically overwritten based solely on `updatedAt` (`diffDays <= 2 ? "on-track" : ...`).
- **Bug**: When a teacher manually resolves or flags a student, `updateStatus()` sets `updatedAt = new Date()`. Consequently, `diffDays` becomes 0, which immediately resets the status back to `"on-track"` on the next load.

### 3.4 Cross-Batch Homework Leakage
- **[practice.index.tsx](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/routes/practice.index.tsx#L30)**:
  `fetchAssignmentsFn()` is invoked with no batch filter. Students in Summer Morning receive assignments meant for Winter Evening or Autumn batches.

### 3.5 Streak Calculation Edge Case
- **[practice.index.tsx](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/routes/practice.index.tsx#L86-L91)**:
  The streak algorithm begins evaluating from `today`. If a student has an ongoing 10-day streak and opens the app at 9:00 AM (before recording their daily attempt), `activeDays.has(today)` is false and the streak immediately renders as `0 days`.

