## 4. Speech, AI & Audio Engine Analysis

### 4.1 Simulated DSP & Random Filler Tagging
- **[audio-analyzer.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/features/practice/lib/audio-analyzer.ts#L61)**:
  ```ts
  if (val >= ACOUSTIC_THRESHOLDS.silence && val < ACOUSTIC_THRESHOLDS.hesitation && Math.random() > 0.6) {
    kind = "filler";
    fillerCount++;
  }
  ```
  Fillers are identified via `Math.random() > 0.6` on low-energy volume samples rather than phoneme classification or speech recognition.
- **[audio-analyzer.ts:L90-L97](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/features/practice/lib/audio-analyzer.ts#L90-L97)**:
  Vocabulary and Grammar scores are derived purely from RMS volume amplitude formulas. There is no natural language grammar parser or ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition) scoring pipeline.

### 4.2 Audio Codec Compatibility on Mobile Safari / iOS
- **[useAudioRecorder.ts](file:///e:/Project/Working/t-trounce/signal-speak-studio-main/src/features/practice/hooks/useAudioRecorder.ts#L174)**:
  MediaRecorder is instantiated without checking `MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported()`. On mobile Safari (iOS), `audio/webm` recording is either unsupported or corrupts playback without an `audio/mp4` fallback.

